{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL407476W","title":"The Story of the Amulet","authors":["Edith Nesbit"],"firstPublished":1905,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #837.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #837","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/837"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1","title":"THE PSAMMEAD"},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2","title":"THE HALF AMULET"},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3","title":"THE PAST"},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4","title":"EIGHT THOUSAND YEARS AGO"},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5","title":"THE FIGHT IN THE VILLAGE"},{"id":"s6","label":"Ch. 6","title":"THE WAY TO BABYLON"},{"id":"s7","label":"Ch. 7","title":"“THE DEEPEST DUNGEON BELOW THE CASTLE MOAT”"},{"id":"s8","label":"Ch. 8","title":"THE QUEEN IN LONDON"},{"id":"s9","label":"Ch. 9","title":"ATLANTIS"},{"id":"s10","label":"Ch. 10","title":"THE LITTLE BLACK GIRL AND JULIUS CAESAR"},{"id":"s11","label":"Ch. 11","title":"BEFORE PHARAOH"},{"id":"s12","label":"Ch. 12","title":"THE SORRY-PRESENT AND THE EXPELLED LITTLE BOY"},{"id":"s13","label":"Ch. 13","title":"THE SHIPWRECK ON THE TIN ISLANDS"},{"id":"s14","label":"Ch. 14","title":"THE HEART’S DESIRE"}],"characters":[{"id":"anthea","name":"Anthea","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It told the children—whose names were Cyril, Robert, Anthea, and Jane—that it was a Psammead or sand-fairy.”"},{"id":"cyril","name":"Cyril","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It told the children—whose names were Cyril, Robert, Anthea, and Jane—that it was a Psammead or sand-fairy.”"},{"id":"jane","name":"Jane","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It told the children—whose names were Cyril, Robert, Anthea, and Jane—that it was a Psammead or sand-fairy.”"},{"id":"robert","name":"Robert","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It told the children—whose names were Cyril, Robert, Anthea, and Jane—that it was a Psammead or sand-fairy.”"},{"id":"psammead","name":"Psammead","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It told the children—whose names were Cyril, Robert, Anthea, and Jane—that it was a Psammead or sand-fairy.”"},{"id":"amulet","name":"Amulet","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““This thing is half of an Amulet that can do all sorts of things; it can make the corn grow, and the waters flow, and the trees bear fruit, and the little new beautiful babies come.”"},{"id":"queen","name":"Queen","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““And maple-framed engravings of the Queen, The Houses of Parliament, the Plains of Heaven, And of a blunt-nosed woodman’s flat return.””"},{"id":"nurse","name":"Nurse","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “So the children were left in the care of old Nurse, who lived in Fitzroy Street, near the British Museum, and though she was always very kind to them, and indeed spoiled them far more than would be good for the most g…”"},{"id":"rekh","name":"Rekh","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: ““Who are these strangers?” Pharaoh asked, and added very crossly, “And what do you mean, Rekh-marā, by daring to come into my presence while your innocence is not established?””"},{"id":"king","name":"King","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: ““From the Empire where the sun never sets, and we want to see your King.””"},{"id":"caesar","name":"Caesar","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““Oh!” said Cyril blushing, “but we only know them to look at, except Latin—and I’m only in Caesar with that.””"},{"id":"pharaoh","name":"Pharaoh","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “As soon as dinner was eaten (it was tinned salmon and lettuce, and a jam tart), and the cloth cleared away, the idea was explained to the others, and the Psammead was aroused from sand, and asked what it thought would…”"},{"id":"pheles","name":"Pheles","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: ““My brother Pheles has just come back from Tarshish.”"},{"id":"imogen","name":"Imogen","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: ““It’s horrible!” she said in a furious whisper, “her father was a carpenter and he was a steady man, and never touched a drop except on a Saturday, and he came up to London for work, and there wasn’t any, and then he…”"},{"id":"britain","name":"Britain","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “It was sunset, and the great man sat on a chair outside his tent gazing over the sea towards Britain—everyone knew without being told that it was towards Britain.”"},{"id":"nisroch","name":"Nisroch","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: ““And the names of their Ministers—perhaps the great Nisroch is one of them?””"},{"id":"st-james-s","name":"St. James’s","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “And I vote we see everything there is, and let’s begin by asking Nurse to give us some bits of bread and we’ll go to St James’s Park.”"},{"id":"pussy","name":"Pussy","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “You quite understand about holding on to the charm as you go through, don’t you, Pussy?””"},{"id":"squirrel","name":"Squirrel","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: ““I _am_ so sorry, poor, dear Squirrel,” said Anthea; “and you were looking so lovely.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"cyril","target":"robert","weight":98,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":6,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s4","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":13},{"at":"s9","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":49}]},{"id":"r2","